\section{Direction is the whole point}{

A bulk download filtered on \code{recipient_search_text} returns subawards where
the queried UEI is the \strong{subawardee}, not the prime. Measured on the
50-nonprofit pilot: of 39,243 subaward rows, \strong{zero} had a prime outside the
pilot paying a subawardee outside it, and zero had a pilot org as prime
paying someone outside. Every row was matched on the subawardee.

So \code{direction == "in"} rows arrive for free and are \emph{additional revenue} not
visible in prime data. \code{direction == "out"} rows -- the pass-through that must
be netted out of revenue -- have to be fetched separately with
\code{\link[=us_fetch_subawards_out]{us_fetch_subawards_out()}}.
